---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site";
---

<Base
  title={"About and editorial policy | " + site.name}
  description={
    "Who publishes " +
    site.name +
    ", how we check our guides, and how our products relate to the advice."
  }
>
  <section class="page-intro wrap narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">About this site</p>
    <h1>
      Useful advice.
      <br />
      Clear ownership.
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      {site.name} is published by the team behind Emisar, Ryker and co:op.
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="prose wrap narrow">
    <h2>Why we publish these guides</h2>
    <p>
      Giving an agent tools creates practical questions. What can it read? What
      can it change? Where should a request stop? Our guides explain the
      controls and the tradeoffs, with examples you can use in your own system.
    </p>
    <p>
      We build products in this area, so we have a commercial interest in some
      of the topics. Product links are labeled, and the{" "}
      <a href="/tools-we-build/">tools we build</a> page explains their
      different roles.
    </p>
    <h2>How we write and check</h2>
    <p>
      Each guide links to the documents behind its technical claims. We prefer
      primary sources: the standard, the project's documentation, or the code
      that owns a behavior. Example policies and records are teaching material.
      They are not reports of a customer's deployment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Review dates mean we checked the article's content. They do not mean we
      ran every vendor product, certified an integration, or tested a production
      system. We label runnable examples, conceptual examples and browser-only
      demonstrations separately.
    </p>
    <h2>Where the advice stops</h2>
    <p>
      A guardrail addresses a defined failure. A policy needs enforcement. A
      sandbox has its own boundary. None of these makes every permitted action
      harmless. Adapt the examples to your assets, permissions and recovery
      procedures.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our governance templates are engineering starting points. Requirements for
      a particular industry, contract or jurisdiction need the right specialist
      review.
    </p>
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The interactive tools run in your browser. They do not send the values you
      enter to us. We do not add analytics, advertising scripts or tracking
      cookies. GitHub Pages serves the site and may process request data under{" "}
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
        GitHub's privacy statement
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <h2>Related reading</h2>
    <p>
      {site.theme === "guardrails" ? (
        <a href="https://aiagentgovernance.dev/">
          AI Agent Governance covers ownership, permissions and operating
          procedures.
        </a>
      ) : (
        <a href="https://aiguardrails.dev/">
          AI Guardrails covers technical checks, failure cases and testing.
        </a>
      )}
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
